From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: reopen a file by name where dup is refused.

This console will not duplicate a descriptor by any means. Measured with four
mechanisms against five descriptor kinds (src/dup-probe): dup, dup2,
fcntl(F_DUPFD) and sceKernelRdup all fail for regular files, directories, shm
objects, sockets and pipes alike. orbis-compat's note that "the descriptor
table is not ours to rearrange" is literal and complete.

dup_fd_object therefore failed, which surfaced four frames away as
release_object(NULL) inside init_directories -- the NLS file mapping, whose fd
it was trying to duplicate.

A file-backed fd does not need duplicating: reopening orig->unix_name gives
exactly what dup would have, an independent descriptor with its own offset and
its own close, and shares nothing. Sockets and pipes have no name and remain
undupable; they have not been reached yet.
---
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index bce9a84f5e..145ad8c51e 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -1879,7 +1879,28 @@ struct fd *dup_fd_object( struct fd *orig, unsigned int access, unsigned int sha
     {
         struct closed_fd *closed = mem_alloc( sizeof(*closed) );
         if (!closed) goto failed;
-        if ((fd->unix_fd = dup( orig->unix_fd )) == -1)
+        fd->unix_fd = dup( orig->unix_fd );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* ⚠ THIS CONSOLE REFUSES TO DUPLICATE A DESCRIPTOR, BY ANY MEANS.
+         * Measured with src/dup-probe: dup, dup2, fcntl(F_DUPFD) and
+         * sceKernelRdup all fail, for regular files, directories, shm objects,
+         * sockets and pipes alike. orbis-compat's "the descriptor table is not
+         * ours to rearrange" is literal and complete.
+         *
+         * A file-backed fd does not need duplicating though: reopening its name
+         * yields what dup would have given -- an independent descriptor with
+         * its own offset and its own close -- without sharing anything. That
+         * covers the callers that matter here, create_file_obj and the mapping
+         * path. A socket or pipe has no name and still cannot be duplicated. */
+        if (fd->unix_fd == -1 && orig->unix_name)
+        {
+            int flags = (orig->access & FILE_WRITE_DATA) ? O_RDWR : O_RDONLY;
+
+            if ((fd->unix_fd = open( orig->unix_name, flags )) == -1 && flags != O_RDONLY)
+                fd->unix_fd = open( orig->unix_name, O_RDONLY );
+        }
+#endif
+        if (fd->unix_fd == -1)
         {
             file_set_error();
             free( closed );
